 ],
 "text": "What if every container ship on earth stopped for 30 days? Around 80% of world trade by volume moves by sea, according to the United Nations. Day 1. Ships drop anchor outside every major port. We've seen a small version of this before. In 2021, 1 ship, the Ever Given, blocked the Suez Canal for 6 days and held up about $9.6 billion of goods every single day. Week 1. Factories start running out of parts. Week 2. Ports go quiet and trucks have nothing to pick up. Month 1. Shelves thin out, prices climb, and every brand finds out how many weeks of stock it really has. How many weeks could your business last? Tell us in the comments."
